          "explanation": "South is on lead with D5432, HJ and CA; North holds DKQJT9 and HA. Leading D2 toward North's honors is feasible, and the retained plan supplies CA for recovery and HJ-to-HA for access after the diamond concession.",
          "quotes": [
            "Start establishing diamonds by leading toward dummy's honors. HJ and HA remain available to reach dummy after DA is dislodged."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0010",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "diamond contest",
          "fact": "DK legally advances the diamond source while preserving access.",
          "explanation": "The authorized trick is D2-D6, and North holds DKQJT9. DK beats D6 unless East plays the unseen DA. If ducked, North can continue diamond honors; South retains HJ and CA opposite North's HA for recovery and entry after DA wins.",
          "quotes": [
            "Play DK to drive out DA, continuing diamonds if it is ducked. HA remains the entry to the established suit."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0011",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "concrete route and trick counting",
          "fact": "CA followed by HJ-to-HA and four diamonds supplies the six additional tricks required.",
          "explanation": "Authorized history shows East winning DA over DK; North now holds DQJT9 and HA. South has HJ and CA facing East's CK lead. CA wins, HJ transfers to HA, and North's four diamonds are all winners. These six tricks added to the three already won make nine.",
          "quotes": [
            "DA is now gone, so win CA and lead HJ to HA. Dummy's four diamond winners then provide the remaining tricks for 3NT."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision-0012",
      "status": "pass",
      "findings": [
        {
          "dimension": "current action and feasible remainder",
          "fact": "C5 follows under CA and preserves a complete route to nine tricks.",
          "explanation": "The authorized current trick is CK-CA-C2, with North holding CT5. C5 legally completes South's winning trick. South retains HJ opposite North's HA and DQJT9, with DA already played; the retained transfer and four diamond winners supply five more tricks after CA, reaching nine.",
          "quotes": [
            "Follow low under CA, then enter dummy with HA and cash its four established diamonds to secure nine tricks."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
